From 5ce1d41803866782bbd96d575f53d43358a20a2e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dhanavandhana Kannan <dhanavandhana.kannan@oss.qualcomm.com>
Date: Fri, 22 Aug 2025 16:32:42 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] nl80211: Fix crash by cancelling scan timeout before a BSS is
 removed

In wpa_driver_nl80211_deinit(), eloop_cancel_timeout() is called to
cancel any pending scan timeouts. However, the scan is typically
initiated using the first BSS context, while the timeout cancellation is
attempted using the last BSS being removed. This mismatch causes the
scan timeout to remain active.

The crash occurs after deinit, when the pending scan_timeout callback is
triggered and attempts to access the BSS context that has already been
freed.

Fix by ensuring that eloop_cancel_timeout() is called before any BSS
links are removed, so the correct context is still valid during
cancellation. Also, reset scan_link to NULL if the link being removed
matches the one used for scanning, preventing access to freed memory.

Signed-off-by: Dhanavandhana Kannan <dhanavandhana.kannan@oss.qualcomm.com>

[backport to 5ace39b0a4cd: this tree has no nl80211_update_active_links()
(2fe31050c248), so the hunk is placed around the existing
"bss->valid_links &= ~BIT(link_id)" line of nl80211_remove_link().

Fixes the hostapd SIGSEGV seen on a mac80211 AP MLD setup when a
hostapd_iface holding a non-first MLD link BSS is removed over the global
control interface ("REMOVE <iface>") while its HT40 coexistence scan
(ieee80211n_check_scan) is still running: the scan was requested for
that link, so bss->scan_link points at its i802_link and the link ctx is
the removed hostapd_data. nl80211_remove_link() cleared the link's
address and valid_links bit but left link->ctx and bss->scan_link, so
the following NL80211_CMD_NEW_SCAN_RESULTS was delivered by
send_scan_event() to the freed hostapd_data
(hostapd_wpa_event() -> switch_link_scan() reading hapd->conf->mld_ap,
drv_callbacks.c:1834). Same scan_timeout hazard as upstream describes.]
Signed-off-by: Petr Štetiar <petr.stetiar@prplfoundation.org>
---
 src/drivers/driver_nl80211.c | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/src/drivers/driver_nl80211.c
+++ b/src/drivers/driver_nl80211.c
@@ -9648,9 +9648,14 @@

 	os_memcpy(link_addr, link->addr, ETH_ALEN);
 	/* First remove the link locally */
-	bss->valid_links &= ~BIT(link_id);
 	os_memset(link->addr, 0, ETH_ALEN);

+	eloop_cancel_timeout(wpa_driver_nl80211_scan_timeout, drv, bss->ctx);
+	bss->valid_links &= ~BIT(link_id);
+
+	if (bss->scan_link == link)
+		bss->scan_link = NULL;
+
 	/* Choose new deflink if we are removing that link */
 	if (bss->flink == link) {
 		for_each_link_default(bss->valid_links, i, 0) {
--
2.51.0
